<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:module:Magento_Config:etc/system_file.xsd">
    <system>
        <section id="zero_personalize" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="99" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
            <label>Recommendations</label>
            <tab>zero</tab>
            <resource>Zero_Personalize::config</resource>
            <group id="status" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="5" showInDefault="1">
                <label>Training</label>
                <field id="panel" type="text" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1">
                    <frontend_model>Zero\Personalize\Block\Adminhtml\Status</frontend_model>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="general" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Recommendations</label>
                <comment><![CDATA[Amazon Personalize learns from the store's orders, carts and wishlists once a week and recommends similar products on the product page and picks for each signed-in customer. It runs in batch mode: AWS bills the training and the batch (a few dollars a run), nothing by the hour.]]></comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Enabled</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>For a website or store view: shows or hides the recommendations there. The weekly training and the exports follow the Default Config value.</comment>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="aws" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1">
                <label>Amazon Personalize</label>
                <comment><![CDATA[The bucket and the role are made once (the module's README has the policies they need). Personalize reads the store's exports from the bucket with the role.]]></comment>
                <field id="region" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Region</label>
                    <validate>required-entry</validate>
                </field>
                <field id="bucket" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>S3 Bucket</label>
                    <comment>In the same region. Each store writes under its own prefix.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="role_arn" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>IAM Role for Personalize</label>
                    <comment>arn:aws:iam::…:role/…, trusted by personalize.amazonaws.com, allowed to read and write the bucket.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="prefix" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="40" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Resource Name Prefix</label>
                    <comment>Empty: "zero-" and the store's host name. Lets one AWS account hold several stores and a development copy.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="access_key" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="50" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Access Key ID</label>
                    <comment>Only for a store outside AWS. Empty: the server's own credentials (the EC2 instance role).</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="secret_key" translate="label" type="obscure" sortOrder="60" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Secret Access Key</label>
                    <backend_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Backend\Encrypted</backend_model>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="training" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1">
                <label>Training</label>
                <field id="mode" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="5" showInDefault="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Training</label>
                    <source_model>Zero\Personalize\Model\Source\TrainMode</source_model>
                    <comment>Each run is billed by AWS (about $1.50–2). By hand, the recommendations stay as the last run left them until Train Now (above) or bin/magento zero:personalize:train.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="day" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Train Every</label>
                    <source_model>Zero\Personalize\Model\Source\TrainDay</source_model>
                    <comment>At night (02:40). A run takes one to three hours.</comment>
                    <depends><field id="mode">schedule</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="lookback_days" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Learn From the Last (days)</label>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <comment>Orders, carts and wishlists of this period.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="customer_days" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Picks for Customers Active in the Last (days)</label>
                    <validate>validate-digits</validate>
                    <comment>0 means the whole "Learn From" period. Each customer is a billed row of the weekly batch: a shorter period costs less. Customers left out see no picks until they are active again.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="max_customers" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="40" showInDefault="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Most Customers per Run</label>
                    <validate>validate-digits</validate>
                    <comment>0 means no limit. Otherwise the most recently active customers come first and the rest are left out.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="batch_results" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="50" showInDefault="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Recommendations per Product and Customer</label>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <comment>From 1 to 12. AWS bills each one. Ask for a few more than the storefront shows: similar products are filtered by department and by what is in stock.</comment>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="storefront" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="40" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Storefront</label>
                <field id="similar_enabled" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Similar Products on the Product Page</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="similar_title" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Similar Products Title</label>
                    <depends><field id="similar_enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="similar_count" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Similar Products Shown</label>
                    <validate>validate-digits validate-digits-range digits-range-1-12</validate>
                    <depends><field id="similar_enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="user_enabled" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="40" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Picks for Signed-in Customers</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>On the home page, the cart and My Account, for customers with a history.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="user_title" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="50" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Picks Title</label>
                    <depends><field id="user_enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="user_count" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="60" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Picks Shown</label>
                    <validate>validate-digits validate-digits-range digits-range-1-12</validate>
                    <depends><field id="user_enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
            </group>
        </section>
    </system>
</config>
